<h1>Accessibility</h1>
<p>
    Wagglesworth Estate is built to meet WCAG 2.2 at the AA level. That's the floor,
    not the goal — if something here doesn't work well for you, it's a bug, not an
    inevitable limitation.
</p>

<h2>What's built in</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Semantic landmarks, one heading per page, and a logical reading and focus order throughout.</li>
    <li>Every control works with the keyboard alone, with a clearly visible focus outline that is never hidden or removed.</li>
    <li>A skip-to-content link at the very start of every page.</li>
    <li>The illustrated Estate map's hotspots are real keyboard-reachable links, and every location is also listed as plain text.</li>
    <li>A text-size control (A−, A+, Reset) that works alongside your browser's own zoom rather than fighting it, and remembers your choice.</li>
    <li>Real, specific alt text on every published image — never a filename, never "image."</li>
    <li>Contrast of at least 4.5:1 for body text and 3:1 for large text and interface elements, tested against this site's specific purple, pink, silver, and cream combinations.</li>
    <li>Motion is gentle and optional, and anything decorative is turned off automatically if you've asked your system for reduced motion.</li>
    <li>No autoplaying audio or video, anywhere.</li>
    <li>Comfortable story-reading columns, generous line spacing, and no justified text.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Still being worked on</h2>
<p>
    This is a first release. Some resident profiles and locations are still marked
    "needs confirmation" rather than filled in with a guess, and a few pieces of
    artwork are generated stand-ins until the originals are found — see the About page
    and this project's public records for the full, honest list.
</p>
